## Steps

### Step 1: File discovery in `src/sweph_file/mod.rs`

Scan `ephe_path` for `.se1` files. Planet files: `sepl_*.se1`, `seplm*.se1`. Moon files: `semo_*.se1`, `semom*.se1`. Open each via `SwissEphFile::open`, collect into `Vec<SwissEphFile>` sorted by `header().tfstart`.

Add a lookup function that finds the right file for a given JD by checking each body's `tfstart/tfend` range:

```rust
pub fn open_ephemeris_files(dir: &Path, prefix: &str) -> Result<Vec<SwissEphFile>, Error> {
    let mut files = Vec::new();
    for entry in std::fs::read_dir(dir).map_err(|_| Error::FileNotFound(dir.to_path_buf()))? {
        let entry = entry.map_err(|_| Error::FileNotFound(dir.to_path_buf()))?;
        let name = entry.file_name();
        let name = name.to_string_lossy();
        if name.starts_with(prefix) && name.ends_with(".se1") {
            files.push(SwissEphFile::open(&entry.path())?);
        }
    }
    files.sort_by(|a, b| a.header().tfstart.partial_cmp(&b.header().tfstart).unwrap());
    Ok(files)
}

pub fn find_file_for_jd<'a>(files: &'a [SwissEphFile], body_id: i32, jd: f64) -> Option<&'a SwissEphFile> {
    files.iter().find(|f| {
        f.planet_data(body_id)
            .map_or(false, |pd| jd >= pd.tfstart && jd <= pd.tfend)
    })
}
```

Prefix matching captures both `sepl_` and `seplm` (both start with `sepl`), and `semo_` and `semom` (both start with `semo`).

