### Step 7: Dispatch and flags_used in `src/context.rs`

Modify `calc_inner` to return `([f64; 24], CalcFlags)` where the second element is the actual ephemeris flag used. Split into `calc_inner_moshier` (existing body match) and `calc_inner_sweph` (new SwissEph dispatch):

```rust
fn calc_inner(&self, jd_tt: f64, body: Body, flags: CalcFlags) -> Result<([f64; 24], CalcFlags), Error> {
    let models = &self.config.astro_models;

    // EclipticNutation, MeanNode, MeanApogee — no backend dependency
    // ... existing code, returning (xreturn, flags) ...

    // Backend dispatch
    match self.config.ephemeris_source {
        EphemerisSource::Swisseph => {
            match self.calc_inner_sweph(jd_tt, body, flags) {
                Ok(result) => Ok(result),
                Err(Error::BeyondEphemerisLimits { .. }) => {
                    // Moshier fallback — update ephemeris flag
                    let ephemeris_flag = (flags & !(CalcFlags::SWIEPH | CalcFlags::JPLEPH)) | CalcFlags::MOSEPH;
                    self.calc_inner_moshier(jd_tt, body, ephemeris_flag)
                }
                Err(e) => Err(e),
            }
        }
        _ => self.calc_inner_moshier(jd_tt, body, flags),
    }
}
```

Update `calc()` to propagate the actual ephemeris flag into `CalcResult.flags_used`.

